Note: EPL GitHub Webhook Server

Create WebApp called github_hook

Route "/webhook" responds with
    Create payload equal to request.data
    If payload is not equal to Nothing then
        Create sender equal to payload.get("sender")
        Create repo equal to payload.get("repository")
        
        Create sender_name equal to "Someone"
        If sender is not equal to Nothing then
            Set sender_name to sender.get("login")
        End
        
        Create repo_name equal to "a repository"
        If repo is not equal to Nothing then
            Set repo_name to repo.get("full_name")
        End
        
        Say "[GitHub] Received webhook from " + sender_name + " for repo " + repo_name

        Note: Extract commit details if available
        Create commits equal to payload.get("commits")
        Create commit_info equal to ""
        If commits is not equal to Nothing then
            If length(commits) > 0 then
                Create latest equal to commits[0]
                Set commit_info to "\n**Commit:** `" + latest.get("message") + "`"
            End
        End
        
        Create message equal to "🚀 **New EPL Update Pushed!**\n\n**Repository:** `" + repo_name + "`\n**Author:** `" + sender_name + "`" + commit_info + "\n\nCheck the latest changes on [GitHub](https://github.com/abneeshsingh21/EPL)!"
        
        Note: Post to #announcements (correct channel) instead of random last-active
        Create announcements_channel equal to "1507812398499893349"
        Create db equal to db_open("agent_memory.db")
        Create embed equal to Map with description = message and color = 1752220
        Create embeds_arr equal to []
        embeds_arr.add(embed)
        Create body equal to json_stringify(Map with embeds = embeds_arr)
        Create token equal to env_get("DISCORD_TOKEN")
        db_execute(db, "INSERT INTO outbound_queue (channel_id, payload, token) VALUES (?, ?, ?)", [announcements_channel, body, token])
        Say "[GitHub] Queued announcement to #announcements."
        
        Send json Map with status = "ok"
    Else
        Send json Map with status = "error"
    End
End

Function run_github_server takes port
    Display "GitHub Webhook Server listening on port " + port
    Start github_hook on port port
End
